# 2279 - echo
# Read all input and output it exactly
# When input becomes 0 (end of stream), halt

# Read character
A<I

# Check if zero - if so, halt
Z<A       # Will halt if A is non-zero... wait, we want opposite!

# We need: if A == 0, then Z = 1
# Strategy: invert the logic
# Set up: B = 1 if A == 0, else B = 0

# Initialize memory
[0]<1     # mem[0] = 1, will be used as halt flag when A==0

# Read and output
A<I
O<A

# Set halt flag based on input
# If A is 0, we want Z = 1
# Use lookup: mem[A] where mem[0] = 1, all others = 0
Z<[A]     # Z = mem[A], so Z = 1 when A = 0

# This should work
